// # oodar/scripts — Build, Test, Verify, Release Entry Points
//
// Logline: The v2.2.0+ scripts/ subdir holds the build, verify, lint, and reproducible-build entry points. The canonical single-TU build is `gcc oodar.c`; the Makefile adds a `liboodar.a` static library artifact, a `lint` target, and per-file compile; the repro_build.sh script produces a bit-identical liboodar.a across builds.
//
// Setup: Per RFC-0005, the canonical four scripts are build, test, verify, and release. The surface covers build (Makefile), lint (Makefile lint* targets), verify (repro_build.sh), and audit (canary_audit.sh); test is in qa/; release is via the governance workflow per rules.oot §1.24. Cap-table drift (caps.h vs cap_table.json) is caught by qa/tests_lint_cap_table via `make lint`, not by generation: the json carries require/grantee metadata with no C source, so no generator can rebuild it.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Makefile              — builds liboodar.a from the umbrella TU; per-file compile; lint targets (lint-anchors, lint-file-size, lint-cap-table).
//   2. repro_build.sh        — reproducible build with SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH, deterministic ar, sorted input, sha256 hash, verify mode.
//   3. canary_audit.sh       — stack-canary coverage audit over liboodar.a (high-risk fns per docs/security_model.oot must be protected).
//   4. double_run.sh         — immune-system half: runs every challenger twice, requires byte-identical output+exit (wired in CI).
//
// ──▓▓ oodar/scripts ANCHOR ──▓▓──
// :: 4 scripts (Makefile 527, repro_build.sh 249, canary_audit.sh 83, double_run.sh 78; the 256 cap gates .oo/.oot/.c/.h only) ::
